// Bandit Level 25 → Level 26

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: Log in to the Bandit Level 25 server:

        ssh bandit25@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step2: Enter the password obtained from Bandit Level 24.

Step3: List the files:

        ls -la

Step4: We can see a private SSH key:

        bandit26.sshkey

Step5: Read the key:

        cat bandit26.sshkey

Step6: Copy the private key to a temporary file on your local machine:

        nano /tmp/bandit26.sshkey

Step7: Paste the private key into the file and save it.

Step8: Set the correct permissions:

        chmod 600 /tmp/bandit26.sshkey

Step9: Try to connect to Bandit Level 26 using the SSH key:

        ssh -i /tmp/bandit26.sshkey bandit26@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step10: Instead of getting a normal shell, the connection immediately closes.

Step11: The reason is that the Bandit 26 user's login shell is not `/bin/bash`. It uses a program called:

        /usr/bin/showtext

Step12: We need to exploit the way the SSH connection starts this program.

Step13: The terminal window must be made very small before connecting.

Step14: Resize the terminal to a very small size.

Step15: Connect again:

        ssh -i /tmp/bandit26.sshkey bandit26@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step16: The `showtext` program opens a text file using `more`.

Step17: Because the terminal is very small, `more` enters its interactive mode instead of immediately exiting.

Step18: Press:

        v

Step19: This opens the file in `vim`.

Step20: Inside `vim`, we can start a shell by entering:

        :set shell=/bin/bash
        :shell

Step21: We now have a shell as `bandit26`.

Step22: Check the current user:

        whoami

Step23: The output should be:

        bandit26

Step24: Read the password for Bandit Level 27:

        cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit26

Step25: The password for Bandit Level 27 is:

        [password returned by the live server]

Step26: The Bandit Level 25 → Level 26 challenge is solved.

Step27: Congratulations!! you have solved this problem!!
